{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Here, between 10 and 11 o'clock on Sunday, having arrived yesterday, I took up quarters at the Hôtel des Princes, — and immediately sought out my cousin. — But here I am overwhelmed by the multitude of great sights I have already seen and traversed, that is to say, from the outside. The Boulevards, the Palais Royal, the Louvre, the Tuileries, the Luxembourg, the Garden and Palace, and so on. — Last evening the Champs Elysées, where the Carousel is, and the taverns, that is to say, the coffee houses, namely those of the Ambassadeur and of the Aurore, — a state of affairs like at the tents, — only ten times more people at the tables, philistines with wives and children, and so forth. — When I walk through the streets, the people look exactly as they do in Berlin, — all dressed in the same way, roughly the same faces, — the same appearance, but in a populous mass."}}],"created":1795219248,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":215,"prompt_tokens":268,"total_tokens":483,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-ervWHv9Y8Xjkbr9zDIpOsooiQ6bTFZWX","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":268,"prompt_ms":510.968,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.9065970149253733,"prompt_per_second":524.4946845986441,"predicted_n":215,"predicted_ms":5065.515,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.670630841121497,"predicted_per_second":42.24644483334863}}